# Licensing

This repository contains several distinct works under different terms. Each
layer is listed separately below. When in doubt, the governing statements are
these; the README, the EPUB colophon, the site footers, and
`docs/api/manifest.json` restate them in shorter form.

---

## 1. The English translation — CC0 1.0 (public domain dedication)

The 12,107 translated verse lines in `translation/book-01.md` through
`translation/book-24.md` — the verse text only, exclusive of the footnote
blocks in those same files — are dedicated to the public domain under
Creative Commons CC0 1.0 Universal.

https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/

To the extent possible under law, the author has waived all copyright and
related or neighboring rights to this translation. You may copy, modify,
distribute, and perform the work, including for commercial purposes, without
asking permission and without providing attribution.

Attribution is not required. It is appreciated, and the suggested form is:

    The Odyssey, translated by Claude (Fable 5), edited by Chris Duffy.
    https://theclaudyssey.com

## 2. The apparatus — CC BY 4.0

Copyright (c) 2026 Chris Duffy. Licensed under Creative Commons
Attribution 4.0 International.

https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

This covers the scholarly apparatus built around the translation:

  - the line notes (the footnote blocks in `translation/book-*.md`)
  - the introduction and other front matter
  - the index of names and places (`index/`)
  - the register of fixed renderings (`FORMULAS.md`)
  - the independence analysis (`docs/independence.html`)

You may share and adapt this material for any purpose, including
commercially, provided you give appropriate credit, link to the license, and
indicate whether changes were made.

## 3. The Greek source text — public domain / CC BY-SA

A. T. Murray's Greek text (Homer: The Odyssey, 2 vols., Heinemann/Putnam,
1919) is in the public domain.

The digitization in `greek/` is from the Perseus Digital Library
(CTS URN `urn:cts:greekLit:tlg0012.tlg002.perseus-grc2`, from the
PerseusDL/canonical-greekLit repository) and is distributed under
CC BY-SA. That attribution is retained for the `greek/` directory and
travels with any redistribution of those files.

https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/

## 4. Embedded font — SIL Open Font License

The EPUB embeds Gentium Plus for polytonic Greek, used under the SIL Open
Font License. The full license text travels with the font in
`epub-build/assets/GentiumPlus-OFL.txt`.

---

## A note on the translation's authorship

The English translation was produced by a large language model (Claude,
Fable 5) under human editorial direction. The EPUB records this in its
EPUB3 creator metadata with MARC relator roles: Homer as author (`aut`),
Claude (Fable 5) as translator (`trl`), Chris Duffy as editor (`edt`).

This is stated plainly here because the CC0 dedication above invites reuse
without attribution, and anyone reusing the text should know what they are
reusing.

## Audio

Audio derived from this text (the generated audiobook) is **not** covered by
the grants above. Its licensing is undetermined at this time. Do not assume
CC0 applies to any recording.
